  "type": "Checkpoint",
  "number": "2.6.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Multiple Response: Which of the following are keywords or will otherwise generate some error from the compiler if used as a variable name?      integer   integer is not a keyword, but int is.     cout   std::cout cannot be used as a variable name!     variable   variable is fair game to use to name a variable.     string   std::string cannot be used as a variable name.     char   char is a keyword and cannot be used as a variable name.    "
