  "title": "",
  "body": "  Finish the code below so that it prints I drive a 2014 Buick Regal   #include <iostream> int main() { std::string make; make = \"Buick\" \/\/ Finish the rest of the assignment statements by assigning \/\/ 2014 and Regal to their respective variables. \/\/ DO NOT MODIFY ANYTHING BELOW THIS LINE. std::cout << \"I drive a \" << year << \" \" << make << \" \"; std::cout << model << std::endl; }    Finish the code below so that it prints I drive a 2014 Buick Regal . Use the lines to construct the pseudocode, then go back to complete the exercise.    Finish the code below so that it prints I drive a 2014 Buick Regal . Use the lines to construct the pseudocode, then go back to complete the exercise.     Open main()    Initialize variable make as string    Assign Buick to make;     Initialize year as int;    Initialize year as double;     Assign a number to year;     Initialize model as string;    Initialize model as char;     Assign model name to model;    Output year and make;    Output model name;    Close main()      "
