  "body": "  Construct a function that takes a dollar amount and cent amount and prints the total amount of money that you have. Hint: the mod operator ‘%' returns the remainder of a division.     void printAmount(int dollars, int cents) {     int dollarTotal = dollars + cents \/ 100;    double dollarTotal = dollars + cents \/ 100.0;      double centTotal = cents % 100;    double centTotal = cents \/ 100;      std::cout << \"$\" << dollarTotal << \".\" << centTotal;    std::cout << \"$\" << dollarTotal << centTotal;     }    "
