  "number": "3.14.yes",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Your final grade is determined by a midterm component (each midterm is worth 20% of the grade) and a final component. In order to avoid any discrepancies with students who's grades are on the fence, your teacher follows this strict grading scale: [0%,60%) = F, [60%, 70%) = D, [70%, 80%) = C, [80%, 90%) = B and [90%, 100%] = A. He does not round until the very end. Construct a function that determines a student's final grade percentage according to this grading scheme and prints the result.      void finalGrade(double m1, double m2, double f) {    void finalGrade(double m1, m2, f) {      double m_comp = m1 * 0.2 + m2 * 0.2;  double f_comp = f * 0.06;    int m_comp = m1 * 0.2 + m2 * 0.2;  int f_comp = f * 0.06;     double final_grade = m_comp + f_comp;     std::cout << int(final_grade);    std::cout << int(final_grade) + 1;     std::cout << final_grade;    }    "
