  "type": "Checkpoint",
  "number": "5.6.3",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  What will print?  int n = 16; int x = 4; bool evenFlag = (n % 2 == 0); bool plusFlag = (x > 0); if (evenFlag) { std::cout << \"n was even when I checked it \"; } if (plusFlag) { std::cout << \"x was positive when I checked it\"; }      n was even when I checked it x was positive when I checked it   Great!     x was positive when I checked it n was even when I checked it   Make sure you follow the correct order of execution. Also, a space is not automatically added.     x was positive when I checked it   Take another look at the result from the modulus operator.     n was even when I checked itx was positive when I checked it   Both flags are made, But A space is after it.     x was positive when I checked itn was even when I checked it   Make sure you follow the correct order of execution.    "
