  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "8.13.8",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  What is the output of the code below?   void foo (int& x, int y) { x = x + 4; y = 2 * x + 3 * y; } void bar(int x, int y) { y = 2 * x; x = x - 1; foo (x, x); } void func(int &x, int& y) { x = x + 3; bar (y, x); } int main() { int x = 4; int y = 7; func (y, x); std::cout << x << \", \" << y; }       4, 7   Take a closer look at func and its parameters. Are they passed by value, passed by reference, or both?     4, 10   Since bar doesn't pass either parameter by reference, neither bar nor foo affect the values of x and y .     7, 7   Check the order of the arguments passed into func .     35, 8   Take a closer look at the three functions. Are they all passed by reference?    "
